  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development and Institutionalization of the Joint Intersectoral Analysis Framework 2022-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Joint Intersectoral Analysis Framework (JIAF) is a methodologically new approach to analyzing the multiple needs of populations in crisis. It is a flagship deliverable of the Grand Bargain, which has been &#x2018;live&#x2019; and used in its first iteration by all countries producing humanitarian needs overviews, since 2020. Once fully developed and institutionalized, the JIAF has the potential to improve the effectiveness of the global humanitarian system, by providing a more rigorous, transparent and people-centered evidence base upon which to plan, fund and respond to populations in crisis.</narrative>
  </description>
